WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.285 --> 00:00:03.174
- [Announcer] Three, two, one!

00:00:03.174 --> 00:00:04.631
(canon explodes)
Blastoff!

00:00:04.631 --> 00:00:08.290
("Entrance of the
Gladiators" by Julius Fucik)

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:11.791
Please welcome our first trapeze in the air,

00:00:11.791 --> 00:00:13.874
the Fabulous Flying Bell!

00:00:16.774 --> 00:00:18.880
(crowd clapping)

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.174
- There's a certain feeling of adrenaline

00:00:21.174 --> 00:00:23.924
once you get up there in the air.

00:00:24.928 --> 00:00:27.787
It's a feeling unlike any other.

00:00:27.787 --> 00:00:30.820
(relaxing music)

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:32.868
You feel power,

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:36.331
you feel like you're in control.

00:00:36.331 --> 00:00:37.748
You feel special.

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:42.715
That's what makes trapeze beautiful.

00:00:42.715 --> 00:00:45.965
That's what makes the circus beautiful.

00:00:50.128 --> 00:00:54.227
My name is Kristin Finley
and I'm a trapeze artist.

00:00:54.227 --> 00:00:57.400
15 years ago I was working
for a brewery in Los Angeles.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.748
I had a great life making great money.

00:00:59.748 --> 00:01:02.628
I had my Lexus and I had a house.

00:01:02.628 --> 00:01:04.628
I was only 24 years old.

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:09.470
A friend of mine told me
that she was flying trapeze.

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:11.031
And I said what are you doing?

00:01:11.031 --> 00:01:13.374
I want to come watch.

00:01:13.374 --> 00:01:16.852
I ended up taking a
class and I was hooked.

00:01:16.852 --> 00:01:19.185
It was addictive right away.

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:24.197
And I quit my life in L.A
and I joined the circus.

00:01:25.268 --> 00:01:27.351
I went from good pay to zero pay.

00:01:27.351 --> 00:01:30.500
Just had to give everything
up pretty much overnight

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:33.337
and here we are 15 years later.

00:01:33.337 --> 00:01:37.858
I never looked back and I've
been on the road ever since.

00:01:37.858 --> 00:01:40.659
(train whistle blowing)

00:01:40.659 --> 00:01:42.041
To run away and join the circus,

00:01:42.041 --> 00:01:43.822
it takes commitment.

00:01:43.822 --> 00:01:45.108
You have to be ready for anything.

00:01:45.108 --> 00:01:47.609
You have to kind of live on your toes

00:01:47.609 --> 00:01:50.425
because you never know
what's going to happen.

00:01:50.425 --> 00:01:53.400
Your own personal space,
your RV or whatever,

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.284
that's your home.

00:01:55.284 --> 00:01:58.617
And that's what has to be stable inside.

00:02:01.251 --> 00:02:02.841
Whenever you're flying trapeze,

00:02:02.841 --> 00:02:04.372
you have to focus on what you're doing.

00:02:04.372 --> 00:02:07.367
And the moment you doubt yourself
in the middle of a trick,

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:08.636
most likely you're gonna mess up.

00:02:08.636 --> 00:02:11.421
You're not gonna make it.

00:02:11.421 --> 00:02:13.043
The fact that I was able to do it

00:02:13.043 --> 00:02:14.350
made it more appealing to me.

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:15.694
And I'm doing these
tricks and they're harder,

00:02:15.694 --> 00:02:19.369
and they're harder, and this is awesome.

00:02:19.369 --> 00:02:21.150
Whatever you want to do
in your wildest dreams,

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:21.983
do it.

00:02:23.001 --> 00:02:23.975
Anything's possible.

00:02:23.975 --> 00:02:26.061
There's not too many African American

00:02:26.061 --> 00:02:28.247
female circus performers,

00:02:28.247 --> 00:02:30.747
but I was still able to do it.

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:33.298
Your life is what you make of it

00:02:33.298 --> 00:02:35.255
and I wouldn't change
my life for the world.

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:36.755
I really wouldn't.

